  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), briefs q01 and q07, CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\n`list_features {\"model\": \"p\", \"kinds\": [\"chains\"], \"compact\": false}` on [q01-2d-plate.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q01-2d-plate/q01-2d-plate.step):\n\n```\nEdge 9  chain:0x60e930a9e55bf92d closed: true length: 321.695 start [60,-34,11.5] end [60,34,11.5]   (perimeter of the 120 x 80 R6 outline is 389.7)\nEdge 12 chain:0x27cd60db24bf8cca closed: true length: 318.554 start [59.5,-34,12] end [59.5,34,12]\nEdge 8  chain:0x4debf4c1532fe7b7 closed: true length: 141.127 start [26,-20,6] end [-26,-20,6]       (pocket loop, true 193.1)\n```\n\nEach is short by exactly the straight segment from `end` back to `start` (68 mm, 68 mm, 52 mm). q07 saw the same (a 838.5 mm loop reported as 768.5). The operations that use the chains still cut the whole loop.\n\n## Expected\n\nA closed chain's length is its full perimeter.\n\nDone means: these three chains report 389.7, 386.6 and 193.1 mm (pinned by a test on a closed chain whose start and end are joined by a straight edge).\n",
